+\begin{statement}{B.24}{Open}{The characteristic-two conjugator-scheme comparison}
+For the Fermat quotient $F_2\to(\Z/2)^2$, the relative completion
+has radical $U_5$, whose abelianization is
+$\Q\oplus\Q[(\Z/2)^2]$. The corresponding integral
+characteristic-two action of the manuscript's signed
+$M_{\rho,\sigma}$ and $N_{\rho,\sigma}$, with every
+infinitesimal parameter, has not been constructed here.
+In particular its kernel and image as group-scheme
+morphisms have not been computed.
+\end{statement}
+The unresolved map is from the signed automorphism
+functor defined by the conjugators and extra generator data
+of \S49 to the automorphism functor of the \emph{relative}
+Fermat completion, preserving its finite quotient and
+peripheral structure. B.8 proves that replacing its radical
+by the absolute $U_2$ loses three abelian dimensions already
+at $n=2$. LM1 E.25, whose explicit dual-number examples
+were reopened, also shows that images of two discrete
+generators alone do not determine this morphism on
+$\F_2[\epsilon]/(\epsilon^2)$: the extra infinitesimal
+parameter must be carried along. The construction
+by word substitution therefore gives a discrete-point
+action only and does not determine the requested functor.
+The first remaining test is that dual-number functor,
+followed by compatibility with the finite quotient's
+nonsemisimple action in characteristic two. The complete
+finite-cover module and Schreier words are supplied by
+B.23; what remains missing is the scheme action.
+
